// The least and the greatest of fractions that a `for` keeps in a unique,
// built for all the cores (Inputs/parallel_bounds.ent): each thread keeps
// its own and the loop's end puts those together as whole numbers in the
// same order (IEEE-754 minimum and maximum: -0 under +0, a NaN kept). The
// same as one core comes to, with any number of threads.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/parallel_bounds.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/parallel_bounds.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
// RUN: env OMP_NUM_THREADS=3 %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/parallel_bounds.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s

// CHECK:      -12500.0 12500.5 0.125 6250.25
// CHECK-NEXT: zeros 9223372036854775808 0
// CHECK-NEXT: nan true true
